From 322bc02867899de1d26cec3348a4636971d97f85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Torben Haack <t128n@ipv4.8shield.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:20:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: background GitHub App polling synchronization

Add outbound-only background polling synchronization for GitHub App installations
without requiring public inbound webhooks.

Key capabilities:
- Implement GitHub App polling worker using RSA PEM authentication and installation tokens
- Add polling schedule manager and durable state transition handlers
- Add database migrations (0079_github_polling.sql for SQLite and Postgres)
- Add web and mobile settings UI to monitor and trigger manual/periodic polling sync
- Support plain HTTP origin registration for GitHub Apps when polling is active
- Generate streamlined GitHub App manifest (omits webhooks and event subscriptions)
- Add concurrency tests and full integration API test suites for background sync
